{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark good traveler to Japan’s fair isle where thy quest doth begin\nUpon the morn of the first day in Tokyo’s bustle thou shalt find thyself\nLose not thy way in Shibuya’s cross where lights do dance and dreams take flight\nThere feast thy eyes on the neon glow and let thy heart be light\nTo Meiji Shrine thou shalt repair where ancient woods do whisper secrets old\nAnd in the garden’s quiet grace let thy weary soul be sold\nEvening shall find thee in Shinjuku where golden statues do stand tall\nAnd in Golden Gai’s narrow lanes the laughter of men shall not grow pallid\n\nOn the morrow take the train swift to Nikko where temples claw the sky\nKegon Falls shall roar in thunder as water from the heavens high\nToshogu Shrine thou shalt behold with gold so bright it doth blind\nAnd through the mossy paths of Kegon Bridge let thy spirit take its kind\nReturn to Tokyo ere the sun doth dip below the horizon’s edge\nAnd in Akihabara’s electric dreams partake of wonders strange and prudge\n\nLo the third day thy ship of dreams shall bear thee to Kyoto’s embrace\nWhere tradition’s breath is warm as teahouse whispers in the place\nFushimi Inari’s torii gates march in endless scarlet row\nAnd through the mountain’s throat thou shalt tread where fox spirits do bestow\nThe Arashiyama Bamboo Grove shall hum a melancholy tune\nWhile the Kinkaku-ji’s golden pavilion shines beneath a heaven’s moon\n\nOn the fourth day to Nara’s ancient halls where deer do graze with grace\nTodai-ji’s giant Buddha watches with a calm and sacred face\nFeed the beasts of gentle mien and let thy heart be filled with cheer\nThen through the parks of Kasuga wander where lanterns softly sear\nEvening finds thee in Osaka’s heart where street food’s siren song doth call\nTake thy fill of takoyaki’s joy and let thy belly feel no thrall\n\nLo the fifth day back to Kyoto where Gion’s lanterns softly sway\nAnd in the teahouse’s quietude sip matcha bright as day\nVisit Kiyomizu’s temple where the stage below doth seem so near\nAnd in the pines of Philosopher’s Path let thy musings take their ear\nBefore thou partest from this land of dreams and ancient lore untold\nBehold the cherry blossoms’ fleeting bloom in spring’s ephemeral gold\n\nThus ends thy journey through Japan’s stage where every act is true\nWith memories carved in temples old and streets alive with hue\nFarewell good traveler till our paths in time do once again meet\nAnd may thy days in fair Japan be as sweet as summer’s heat.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.1340528428554535}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0033846967853605747}, {"token": " good", "logprob": -2.1330671310424805}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.5294211506843567}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0005539313424378633}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.1349453926086426}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -1.025579571723938}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.5305728316307068}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.19100317358970642}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -1.7687616348266602}, {"token": "le", "logprob": -0.07042431086301804}, {"token": " where", "logprob": -0.4350681006908417}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -1.7584991455078125}, {"token": " quest", "logprob": -1.452800989151001}, {"token": " d", "logprob": -0.6589934229850769}, {"token": "oth", "logprob": -5.447716102935374e-05}, {"token": " begin", "logprob": -0.7204857468605042}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.29178673028945923}, {"token": "Upon", "logprob": -1.8511347770690918}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.13692402839660645}, {"token": " morn", "logprob": -0.8899091482162476}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.059708114713430405}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.4345741271972656}, {"token": " first", "logprob": -0.4228648245334625}, {"token": " day", "logprob": -0.06253575533628464}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -2.041473388671875}, {"token": " Tokyo", "logprob": -0.4